MID_EV11_032_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_032_m01_001: Aurora. I've brought your son.
MID_EV11_032_m01_002: Cai! Your left hand, is it alright? Has anything else\nout of the ordinary happened?
MID_EV11_032_m01_047: It's fine, I think. It hasn't been doing anything\nstranger than usual.
MID_EV11_032_m01_003: Did you find out anything about it? Is that why you\nwanted to see me?
MID_EV11_032_m01_004: Actually, Cai, I have a favor to ask of you.
MID_EV11_032_m01_005: We might be able to resolve some questions around\nthat jewel if we find out how my father got it.
MID_EV11_032_m01_006: But my hands are tied here, and Castor is...\nawaiting execution. Ugh!
MID_EV11_032_m01_007: If I only had the liberty to act!
MID_EV11_032_m01_048: <NCA>Remember something.
MID_EV11_032_m01_009: You know, in one match, I fought next to someone\nwho had a power like mine.
MID_EV11_032_m01_010: Theodora, queen of Saramis.
MID_EV11_032_m01_011: She was really strong and kinda scary. She could\ncrush a weapon in her hand.
MID_EV11_032_m01_012: Interesting. There's such a person fighting in the\ngames? I'd love to see that.
MID_EV11_032_m01_013: Not long after that, I ran into someone who said the\njewel is one of Drake's treasures.
MID_EV11_032_m01_014: She was a mysterious woman named Anatolia. She\nsaid the treasures give you power and a curse.
MID_EV11_032_m01_018: I know something of them. Drake's treasures first\nappeared about five hundred years ago.
MID_EV11_032_m01_019: Drake, a pirate, used their power to rule the\nDanann Sea.
MID_EV11_032_m01_020: It's believed that, after his death, the treasures were\nscattered across Dagda.
MID_EV11_032_m01_021: Your red jewel may well be one of these\ntreasures, Cai.
MID_EV11_032_m01_022: As it happens, an old friend of mine has some \nknowledge on this subject. Should we consult him?
MID_EV11_032_m01_023: Certainly. But I, too, have some ideas about the true\nnature of Drake's treasures.
MID_EV11_032_m01_024: What do you mean?
MID_EV11_032_m01_025: I have long hoped to confirm them, but alas, I cannot\nleave this place.
MID_EV11_032_m01_026: Cai, since you're now strong enough to earn victory\nin the games, I feel I can entrust this task to you.
MID_EV11_032_m01_027: This could be very important for both of us, son.
MID_EV11_032_m01_028: What do you need me to do?
MID_EV11_032_m01_029: To the south, near Saraminian lands, there is a place\ncalled the Isle of Sorrows.
MID_EV11_032_m01_030: On the isle sits a temple, which I believe to be the\nburial place of my grandfather.
MID_EV11_032_m01_031: Cai, I want you to go there and see it with your\nown eyes.
MID_EV11_032_m01_033: Aurora, travel is restricted in those lands, in light of\nthe Damascar incident.
MID_EV11_032_m01_049: Perhaps one could pass the checkpoint with my\npermission and vulkan authority?
MID_EV11_032_m01_034: What I'm saying is I'd like you to accompany\nhim, Centurio.
MID_EV11_032_m01_035: Understood! I swear on my sobriquet, Corundum,\nthat I will protect the boy.
MID_EV11_032_m01_036: But I implore you, take the Gate of the Gods.\nYou'll get to your destination much more quickly.
MID_EV11_032_m01_037: This is my...great-grandpa's grave we're talking\nabout here.
MID_EV11_032_m01_038: Guess I better get ready. A trip will be fun, right?
MID_EV11_032_m01_039: I'd like to go there myself, but Centurio here won't\nallow me to leave the temple.
MID_EV11_032_m01_040: It's true. By order of the Divine Sovereign himself.
MID_EV11_032_m01_041: But this is important, damn you! How can you be\nso inflexible?
MID_EV11_032_m01_042: Excuse me. If it pleases you, may I accompany your\nson too?
MID_EV11_032_m01_043: I'm from the Callisto region myself, so I know of the\narea. I also know some recovery magic.
MID_EV11_032_m01_044: Really? It'll be even more fun if you're coming.
MID_EV11_032_m01_045: Thank you, Ultand. Yes, I'll entrust Cai and his\nfriends to you as well.
MID_EV11_032_m01_046: But listen to me. I want you to come right back here\nif there's any sign of danger. Understand?
MID_EV11_033_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_033_m01_001: This is what is known as a Gate of the Gods.\nIt's probably new to you, isn't it?
MID_EV11_033_m01_002: Yeah. I can feel some kind of mysterious power\ncoming from it. It's a doorway but...more.
MID_EV11_033_m01_003: Through this, you'll be transported to the primary\ntemple of Aurora in a single step.
MID_EV11_033_m01_004: That's in the Melias region! If we traveled normally,\nit would take forever!
MID_EV11_033_m01_005: Um... Ultand, by any chance is the thought of this\ntrip making you nervous?
MID_EV11_033_m01_006: W-well, it's just... I've never used one of these\nthings before.
MID_EV11_033_m01_007: Originally, these devices were set aside for the\nexclusive use of the gods.
MID_EV11_033_m01_008: Now, even among the priests, their use is limited to a\nselect few.
MID_EV11_033_m01_009: Hard to believe I get to experience something so\nvery exclusive... Oh, I'm excited!
MID_EV11_033_m01_010: Tialla's curious as ever. Me, I'm just scared.
MID_EV11_033_m01_011: Now, everyone, move toward the center of the circle\non the floor.
MID_EV11_033_m01_012: And here we are. You may step out now.
MID_EV11_033_m01_013: What? We're here already?! That was even faster\nthan I imagined!
MID_EV11_033_m01_014: You sure we moved? You're not messing with us, are\nyou, Centurio?
MID_EV11_033_m01_015: There was a bright, white glow all around us. I got a\nlittle fluttery sensation, but that was it.
MID_EV11_033_m01_016: The air feels strange on my skin. And the smells\nhere... It's all different from Dagsion.
MID_EV11_033_m01_017: Assuredly, we are in the primary temple of Aurora.
MID_EV11_033_m01_018: Halt! Who goes there?!
MID_EV11_033_m01_019: Corundum Centurio. Chief celestial general of\nAurora's temple vulkans.
MID_EV11_033_m01_020: We're here on the direct order of Aurora herself.\nYou may step down.
MID_EV11_033_m01_021: Centurio! Sir! Forgive us! We didn't mean to get in\nthe way of your mission.
MID_EV11_033_m01_022: That settles it for me. In the temple I know, I've\nnever seen those guards.
MID_EV11_033_m01_023: Cai, is something troubling you?
MID_EV11_033_m01_024: It's just... I thought you were this serious, uptight\nsoldier type.
MID_EV11_033_m01_025: But I'm realizing...these temple folks really\nadmire you.
MID_EV11_033_m01_026: It comes with the rank, but I like to think I've\nearned it. Seems like you're coming around too!
MID_EV11_082_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_082_m01_001: This is an old road known as the Pilgrim's Path.\nIf we keep going, we'll reach Cybele. 
MID_EV11_082_m01_002: For a road with such a nice name, it's awfully creepy.
MID_EV11_082_m01_003: Anyone else getting a "go no farther" feeling?
MID_EV11_082_m01_004: Technically, this is imperial territory. But, yeah, it's\ngot a strange feel to it.
MID_EV11_082_m01_006: This road once lead to Ahm Lu, capital of the fallen\nkingdom of Damascar.
MID_EV11_082_m01_032: <NCA>Ask about Damascar.
MID_EV11_082_m01_007: Damascar? What kind of place was that?
MID_EV11_082_m01_008: Oh, I read all about Damascar in one of\nGrandpa's books.
MID_EV11_082_m01_009: There was once a temple to Yu Phas,\nAurora's mother.
MID_EV11_082_m01_010: The people were devout followers of Yu Phas.
MID_EV11_082_m01_011: And then the Dagdan Empire destroyed the entire\ncountry in a single night.
MID_EV11_082_m01_012: It's hard to believe something like that could happen.\nHow does such an awful event come about?
MID_EV11_082_m01_013: That was the Cleansing of Damascar. As to how it\nhappened, nothing remains in temple records.
MID_EV11_082_m01_014: What's more, Damascar had no written language, so\nthere are no historical manuscripts about the event.
MID_EV11_082_m01_015: The lands have been cast aside, abandoned\nfor centuries.
MID_EV11_082_m01_016: The attackers razed the royal capital Ahm Lu. It has\nbecome a city of death, and no one ventures near.
MID_EV11_082_m01_018: Centurio! What is that?!
MID_EV11_082_m01_019: Ultand!
MID_EV11_082_m01_020: Yes! Got it! Hyah!
MID_EV11_082_m01_021: C-C-Centurio... Wh-what was that thing?
MID_EV11_082_m01_022: A gh-gh-ghost?
MID_EV11_082_m01_023: Aye. I hazard it was the spirit of a slain citizen of\nDamascar, wandering aimlessly.
MID_EV11_082_m01_024: Ironic that a road for pilgrims ends up a highway for\nthe dead.
MID_EV11_082_m01_025: Road's dead, land's dead, but the dead are awake.
MID_EV11_082_m01_026: We'll encounter more of them as we move on.\nBut there's something else.
MID_EV11_082_m01_027: The remnants of the Damascar people. Their\ndescendants are forest dwellers, often violent.
MID_EV11_082_m01_028: Among them, those known as the Har Hali are\nfiercely warlike.
MID_EV11_082_m01_029: We should avoid them at all costs. But don't fret\nabout them.
MID_EV11_082_m01_030: I, Centurio, will protect all of you, with my own life\nshould it come to that.
MID_EV11_082_m01_031: For now, we must continue along the road toward\nAhm Lu. The Isle of Sorrows is near there.
MID_EV11_113_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_113_m01_001: What's this? Such a huge picture.
MID_EV11_113_m01_002: It's a mural done in the Damascar style, I believe.\nI've never seen one as grand as this.
MID_EV11_113_m01_003: B-but this image... What's it about?
MID_EV11_113_m01_004: It looks like a bunch of people are getting tossed into\na big...lake?
MID_EV11_113_m01_005: Men, women, kids. Everyone.
MID_EV11_113_m01_006: And the ones looking down on it from above...
MID_EV11_113_m01_007: This... It can't be... It is!
MID_EV11_113_m01_008: Tialla, do you know about this?
MID_EV11_113_m01_009: I'm pretty sure I read about this in one of Grandpa's\nmany books.
MID_EV11_113_m01_010: Dagda's cauldron... It was said to be a huge, awful\nexecution device in old Dagsion.
MID_EV11_113_m01_011: Uh... Execution device?
MID_EV11_113_m01_012: Yes. It was enormous, much bigger than a house\nand made of orichalcum.
MID_EV11_113_m01_013: Dagsion used it to punish those who committed\nserious crimes...or defied the Emperor.
MID_EV11_113_m01_014: Thousands, maybe tens of thousands, were cast into\nit. They basically...melted to death.
MID_EV11_113_m01_015: I've heard this story too. Naughty kids who don't\nlisten to their parents...
MID_EV11_113_m01_016: Soldiers snatch 'em up, toss 'em in the pot, and stew\n'em till tender. Then the Emperor gobbles 'em up.
MID_EV11_113_m01_017: That's what parents in the empire tell their children\nas a warning to behave.
MID_EV11_113_m01_018: I thought it was pure fiction. I never believed\nsomething like this might have actually existed.
MID_EV11_113_m01_019: B-but I haven't seen anything like this in Dagsion.\nHave you?
MID_EV11_113_m01_020: Kinda strange that something so huge would just\ndisappear, right?
MID_EV11_113_m01_021: I have heard that when the Emperor began his deep\nsleep, the Divine Sovereign hid the cauldron.
MID_EV11_113_m01_022: It was this cauldron that took Yu Phas's life. So I\nsuppose he didn't want to look upon it ever again.
MID_EV11_113_m01_023: Hid the cauldron...somewhere in Dagsion?
MID_EV11_113_m01_024: That horrible thing still exists?!
MID_EV11_113_m01_025: I believe so. I've never seen any record of it having\nbeen dismantled.
MID_EV11_113_m01_026: It must remain intact somewhere in Dagsion, out\nof sight.
MID_EV11_113_m01_027: Yu Phas... That means...my grandmother...ended up\nin this thing.
MID_EV11_034_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_034_m01_001: That shoreline we can see there, perhaps it's the\nIsle of Sorrows, but...
MID_EV11_034_m01_002: D-does anyone else think that island is a little too\ncreepy to investigate?
MID_EV11_034_m01_030: <NCA>Observe the island.
MID_EV11_034_m01_003: You can make out some nicer buildings there.\nMust be the temple my mom mentioned.
MID_EV11_034_m01_004: That is indeed the Isle of Sorrows, also known as the\nIsle of Balor.
MID_EV11_034_m01_005: It is dedicated to Yu Phas's father, the demon god.
MID_EV11_034_m01_006: That would be...your great-grandfather.
MID_EV11_034_m01_007: Demon god Balor? King of the underworld?
MID_EV11_034_m01_008: If that's true, that island's probably the scariest place\nin the entire world. Right?
MID_EV11_034_m01_009: Centurio, are you sure this is going to be alright?\nPerhaps it's too risky.
MID_EV11_034_m01_010: If it's like my mom says and the secrets of Drake's\ntreasures are on that island...
MID_EV11_034_m01_011: I'm going.
MID_EV11_034_m01_012: If that's what you want, your faithful Centurio will\naccompany you.
MID_EV11_034_m01_013: Yep. If Cai's going, I'm going.
MID_EV11_034_m01_014: Peter, you want to wait here? Alone?
MID_EV11_034_m01_015: That's not even a little funny. Don't you dare leave\nme by myself.
MID_EV11_034_m01_016: Great. So how do we get over there?
MID_EV11_034_m01_017: I... I can't swim.
MID_EV11_034_m01_018: We're mountain kids, not sea kids.
MID_EV11_034_m01_019: I can swim just fine, but that's way too far.
MID_EV11_034_m01_020: Let's search nearby hamlets. Maybe we'll find a\nseaworthy vessel.
MID_EV11_034_m01_021: Gaaa! Another ghost!
MID_EV11_034_m01_022: Settle down, Peter. Does that look like a ghost\nto you?
MID_EV11_034_m01_023: Ngh!
MID_EV11_034_m01_024: You defile our sacred land with your filthy feet...\nDo not imagine you'll leave here alive.
MID_EV11_034_m01_025: Who are you?! Your threats make you an enemy!
MID_EV11_034_m01_026: We're surrounded! How...
MID_EV11_034_m01_027: Cai usually has a good sense for danger. How did\nthey get past him?
MID_EV11_034_m01_028: No. It can't be. Har Hali warriors!
MID_EV11_034_m01_029: For the sin of striding onto Balor's sacred grounds,\nyour souls are forfeit.
MID_EV11_035_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_035_m01_001: Victory is yours. Do as you will with our souls.
MID_EV11_035_m01_002: We'd rather not kill you if that's an option.
MID_EV11_035_m01_003: We would like some answers though. What can you\ntell us about the kingdom of Damascar?
MID_EV11_035_m01_004: Specifically, where did the people come from?\nAnd what happened to them?
MID_EV11_035_m01_005: To understand Damascar, one must first understand\nthe People of the White Egg.
MID_EV11_035_m01_037: <NCA>Ask about the People of the White Egg.
MID_EV11_035_m01_038: The People of the White Egg? I don't think I've\nheard of them.
MID_EV11_035_m01_006: They lived in a land far to the west, in a corner of\nthe desert.
MID_EV11_035_m01_007: There was an awesome battle between the People of\nthe White Egg and the Dagdan Empire.
MID_EV11_035_m01_009: It was a long, fierce war, like a sundering of land\nand sky. The empire defeated the White Egg.
MID_EV11_035_m01_010: They took a hundred thousand souls to Dagsion and\ncruelly put them to death in Dagda's cauldron.
MID_EV11_035_m01_011: That must be the scene we saw on the mural in\nthe settlement.
MID_EV11_035_m01_012: The goddess Yu Phas, distraught, begged Dagda the\nGreat for their salvation.
MID_EV11_035_m01_013: She saved five thousand prisoners, young boys\nand girls.
MID_EV11_035_m01_014: Yu Phas herself led their migration to this land and\nhelped them develop and cultivate it.
MID_EV11_035_m01_015: Eventually, the state known as Damascar grew forth,\na tender sapling in this soil.
MID_EV11_035_m01_039: Interesting. Hard to imagine something like that\nhappening here.
MID_EV11_035_m01_016: However, in time, the Dagdan Empire stamped out\nthat sapling too.
MID_EV11_035_m01_017: They laid siege to the royal city and then destroyed\neverything, even the keep and the temple of Yu Phas.
MID_EV11_035_m01_018: The empire's soldiers were wholly without mercy.\nThey beheaded the members of the royal line.
MID_EV11_035_m01_019: Men, women, young, and old fled in panic. But the\nempire slaughtered them all and set the world ablaze.
MID_EV11_035_m01_040: That's awful... Why was Dagda the Great so angry?
MID_EV11_035_m01_041: The reasons are obscure, even to the historians.\nThat's because no official record remains.
MID_EV11_035_m01_020: At that time, the empire executed blessed Yu Phas.\nSince then, our people have hated the gods of Dagda.
MID_EV11_035_m01_021: But we hold Yu Phas and her father, demon god\nBalor, sacred in our hearts.
MID_EV11_035_m01_022: Balor, who boasted of a power that surpassed even\nthat of Dagda...
MID_EV11_035_m01_023: became an object of reverence for the Har Hali\npeople, worshippers of strength and power.
MID_EV11_035_m01_027: Can you provision us with a boat? We need to survey\nthat island.
MID_EV11_035_m01_028: Absurd. Do not approach that island. You must not\neven consider it.
MID_EV11_035_m01_029: It's a place of contradiction. It's empty but also...\noccupied...by something terrifying.
MID_EV11_035_m01_030: To go there is to brush against Balor, a truly\nhorrifying proposition.
MID_EV11_035_m01_031: This young boy is the blood heir of Yu Phas, whom\nyou so revere.
MID_EV11_035_m01_032: What? You're... Is this true?
MID_EV11_035_m01_033: It is. Yu Phas is my grandmother. That makes Balor\nmy great-grandfather.
MID_EV11_035_m01_034: Please, friend, get us to that island.
MID_EV11_035_m01_035: Hmm... *sigh*
MID_EV11_035_m01_036: A direct request from a descendant of Yu Phas...\nAs denizens of the forest, how can we refuse?
MID_EV11_079_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_079_m01_001: It's just an empty sarcophagus. It seems something\nwas once enshrined here though.
MID_EV11_079_m01_002: Look! Here on the floor. There are some faint lines.\nSomething heavy was dragged here, maybe?
MID_EV11_079_m01_003: Or dragged out of here, I guess. Probably explains\nwhy there's nothing around.
MID_EV11_079_m01_004: Oh! What's this awful mural?
MID_EV11_079_m01_005: It's...a man... He's being torn apart!
MID_EV11_079_m01_006: I'm feeling... What is this? I've felt it before...
MID_EV11_079_m01_010: Haaah... Ngh...
MID_EV11_079_m01_011: Urk...
MID_EV11_079_m01_012: Oh! Cai! Are you alright?
MID_EV11_079_m01_013: AAAAAH! My hand is burning!
MID_EV11_079_m01_014: Cai! Everyone, look! His eyes!
MID_EV11_079_m01_015: Cai! What's going on?!
MID_EV11_079_m01_016: Cai! Are you alright?!
MID_EV11_079_m01_017: Aaaah!
MID_EV11_079_m01_018: Hng... Haaah...
MID_EV11_079_m01_019: Huh? Where...am I? Where'd everyone go?
MID_EV11_036_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_036_m01_001: Cai, your eyes changed color! What's happened?!
MID_EV11_036_m01_002: We were in Balor's temple, and...they just changed.\nThey haven't gone back to normal since.
MID_EV11_036_m01_003: No, I mean they're a wonderful color. Just like your\ngrandma Yu Phas's eyes.
MID_EV11_036_m01_004: Everyone, I am truly sorry. It sounds as though I put\nyou in some very grave danger.
MID_EV11_036_m01_006: It was one creepy adventure, but... Mom, who was\nBalor? Other than my great-grandfather, that is.
MID_EV11_036_m01_007: This is nothing more than a story I heard from my\nfather as a child, but I'll tell you.
MID_EV11_036_m01_008: This takes place a long, long time ago, more than\n10 thousand years past.
MID_EV11_036_m01_009: A being called the progenitor god came to the land.\nThat event set everything in motion.
MID_EV11_036_m01_010: She divided her power, first to the seven pillars, the\nfounding gods, then to their many descendants.
MID_EV11_036_m01_011: The seven pillars, who came first, had the greatest\npower of all, so they were called "Founders."
MID_EV11_036_m01_012: My grandfather, Balor of the Ashes, was a Founder.\nHis power was truly awesome.
MID_EV11_036_m01_013: At some point, he went to war against the progenitor\ngod and her descendants.
MID_EV11_036_m01_014: Balor's power was overwhelming, but in the end, the\nprogenitor god subdued him.
MID_EV11_036_m01_015: She divided his body into eight pieces and interred\nhim in the crypt on the Isle of Sorrows.
MID_EV11_036_m01_016: Dagda the Great sealed the entrance and posted\nsentinels to guard it.
MID_EV11_036_m01_017: Those sentinels were the daughters of Balor—my\nmother, Yu Phas, and her sisters.
MID_EV11_036_m01_018: But as you saw, Cai, the tomb is empty now.\nThat can only mean one thing.
MID_EV11_036_m01_019: Someone broke the seal and carried away\nBalor's remains.
MID_EV11_036_m01_020: What's more, the sentinels are missing and probably\nhave been for a long time.
MID_EV11_036_m01_021: It's unlikely that the temples are ignorant of these\nfacts. I assume they've purposely concealed them.
MID_EV11_036_m01_022: So...this red jewel is really...
MID_EV11_036_m01_023: This is nothing more than a feeling, but I do think it\nmight be part of my grandfather's remains.
MID_EV11_036_m01_024: Wha— A piece of a corpse can have that\nmuch power?
MID_EV11_036_m01_026: I wonder if the jewel in Cai's hand is what's left of\none of my grandfather's eyes.
MID_EV11_036_m01_028: For such power to persist so long after he died...
MID_EV11_036_m01_029: Perhaps Balor's resentment has not diminished\nbut grown stronger with time.
MID_EV11_036_m01_030: Cai, what you saw with your own eyes might have\nbeen the underworld, Balor's domain.
MID_EV11_036_m01_031: Extraordinary hatred must have empowered \nunderworld forces around Balor's tomb.
MID_EV11_036_m01_034: I have to wonder about the being who came to our\naid, the Herald of the Pale Raven.
MID_EV11_036_m01_035: Not even the merest mention of such a person is\nfound in the records.
MID_EV11_036_m01_036: But surely, they cannot be evil. I will need to thank\nthis unexpected guardian for saving you.
MID_EV11_037_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_037_m01_001: Hmmm...
MID_EV11_037_m01_002: Mm? What's wrong, Sister?
MID_EV11_037_m01_003: Quiet! She's hearing Father's voice!
MID_EV11_037_m01_004: Hm? Has something happened? To Father?
MID_EV11_037_m01_005: Unclear. But it seems someone has violated\nBalor's temple.
MID_EV11_037_m01_006: The underworld nearly manifested there, though it\nwould never have extended past the temple's interior.
MID_EV11_037_m01_007: The underworld is the inner dimension of Father's\nsoul, an alternate realm empowered by his spirit.
MID_EV11_037_m01_008: Father's influence has long been confined to his\ntemple, where his remains were put to rest.
MID_EV11_037_m01_009: Nowhere in the world can the underworld manifest\nso easily as there.
MID_EV11_037_m01_010: Though "easy" is relative. It is still exceedingly\nunlikely. For it to almost happen anyway means...
MID_EV11_037_m01_011: Father's power has gotten even stronger than we\nthought it would, hasn't it?
MID_EV11_037_m01_012: We might need to hurry our plans for bringing his\nunderworld to these lands.
MID_EV11_037_m01_013: But would mere mortals breaking into the tomb\ncreate such a disturbance?
MID_EV11_037_m01_014: For Father to resonate so deeply with them...\nWhoever could they have been?
MID_EV11_037_m01_015: You don't think... Could it have been the girl with\nour sister's blood in her veins?
MID_EV11_037_m01_016: No... Aurora is confined within her temple. I do not\nthink she can freely leave.
MID_EV11_037_m01_017: *gasp*
MID_EV11_037_m01_018: Mahna, do you have an idea who this person is?
MID_EV11_037_m01_019: No... It's nothing. Pay me no mind.
MID_EV11_037_m01_020: It can't be... Is it that wretched child who shares my\nblood? No... No, that's far too ridiculous a notion.